// "PowerAndToughness" = the single-op power-and-toughness bundler: one
// `NumericOp` applied to BOTH axes at once ([CR#613.4] layer 7). A
// `Modification`-kind macro that stands as the single change in a
// `Modify(It, …)` — `PowerAndToughness(Up(2))` is Elesh Norn's "+2/+2",
// `PowerAndToughness(Down(2))` her "-2/-2". A macro expands to ONE value, so
// the two axis ops bundle in a `Several`; `Modification::flatten` splices it
// away at the engine boundary. Unlike `AddPowerToughness(p, t)` (two `Count`
// magnitudes, always `Up`), this takes ONE `NumericOp` (`Up`/`Down`/`Set`)
// shared by both axes — the symmetric case where power and toughness move
// together.
(
    name: "PowerAndToughness",
    template: "gets ${0}/${0}",
    kinds: [Modification],
    params: [NumericOp],
    body: Several([Power(Param(0)), Toughness(Param(0))]),
)
